+def reallocate_adjacent_portal_once(path, chain, allocation, containment):
+    """Return one deterministic adjacent-portal reallocation or ``None``.
+
+    C3 rework 01 allows exactly one fixed-sigma recovery: when a hard
+    continuous-containment failure is located at the switch between two
+    adjacent corridors, move that single switch boundary to the midpoint of
+    the connected path-parameter interval that lies inside *both* corridors'
+    original halfspaces.  A width-limit failure may occur where the path
+    leaves its assigned corridor just before the true two-corridor overlap;
+    that is accepted only when the failure hugs or crosses the assigned
+    halfspace boundary and the old switch itself lies in the overlap.  An
+    interior containment failure that is not at the halfspace boundary is
+    never treated as a fixed-sigma switch failure.  No other boundary,
+    corridor order or allocation entry is changed.
+
+    This function is a candidate generator, not a certificate.  It checks the
+    two original halfspace sets directly on the real path model (never a
+    sparse collision approximation), then calls the existing
+    ``validate_corridor_allocation`` before returning.  The new allocation
+    must still pass the NLP, continuous containment and every downstream
+    geometry/dynamics/collision audit.  ``None`` means no legal candidate was
+    available and the caller must keep the original fail-closed result.
+    """
